# NET G cell — the STAGE-1-ONLY class. list/vector arm.
#
# AXIS CELL: comp-kind = list `[...]`  ·  source = String (codepoints)  ·
# destination = `auto` (the EMPTY result channel)  ·  FILTERED.
#
# ⚠ THIS CELL EXISTS BECAUSE NO ORDINARY GATE CAN SEE ITS CLASS. Every
# self-host gate in the tree runs the STAGE-0 driver (the one Rust gg built),
# and `self_host_bootstrap_fixed_point` compares emitted C *text*, not
# behaviour.
#
# THE ABLATION, MEASURED. On a pristine-HEAD stage-1 binary this cell is
# rc 101 printing `0`; the SAME HEAD driver at stage 0 prints the correct
# `2/a`. The round's rework of the filter path takes stage 1 to `2/a`.
#
# THE MECHANISM, PINNED — and it is NOT "a boxed parameter". The self-host
# lowerer DOUBLE-FREES on `(*b).clone()` where `b` was bound by
# `case Some(b)` on an `Option[Box[T]]`; the pre-fix filter path spelled
# exactly `(*filt_box).clone()`, so a driver compiled BY THE SELF-HOST
# corrupted the heap on every FILTERED comprehension while a driver compiled
# by Rust gg did not. Durable repro, RED on the self-host lane at rc 134 and
# correct on Rust: `known_gaps/sh_option_box_deref_clone_double_free.gg`
# (`known_gap_sh_option_box_deref_clone_double_free`). Filed in `TODO.md`
# (grep `stage-1-only`) — the compiler defect itself is UNFIXED.
#
# ⚠ WHAT ACTUALLY HAS TO STAY IS THE ABSENCE OF `(*box).clone()` ON THE
# FILTER PATH — not this cell's flattened signature. All three arms now
# clone a PLAIN value (`filt_e.clone()` in `comp_synth_body_bound`), and the
# set/dict arms KEEP the `Option[Box[SpannedExpr]]` parameter and unpack it
# with a bare `*fb`, which is measured green at stage 1. So the boxed
# parameter was never the hazard; the clone-through-a-match-bound-Box was.
# Re-demonstrated by a one-line ablation: change the set arm's
# `sv_fe = *sv_fb` to `sv_fe = (*sv_fb).clone()` and
# `self_host_comprehension_stage1_net` goes RED on `stage1_set_strsrc_filt`
# (`0/false/false` for `2/true/true`) while all 39 stage-0 cells stay green.
#
# ⚠ Earlier triage ran four probes of the boxed-option-through-a-parameter
# shape and found them all CORRECT. They were correct: none of them cloned
# the deref. That is why the attribution stood unproven for a round — the
# probe set sampled the parameter axis and not the operator axis.
#
# The wired test `self_host_comprehension_stage1_net` builds a STAGE-1
# binary and runs this cell through it — that is the only instrument in the
# tree that sees this class.
#
# The `.len()` assertion is KEPT beside the element read on purpose: for this
# class the LENGTH is the observable (a dropped filter changes the count),
# while the element read is what catches a mint defect.
#
# RED-VERIFIED: stage 0 at HEAD is GREEN (`2/a`) — this cell's RED lives ONLY
# at stage 1, where a pristine-HEAD stage-1 binary is rc 101 printing `0`.
#
# FIXTURE PLACEMENT: subdirectory (see any NET A cell's header).
# LANE: self-host only.  STAGE: 0 AND 1.  RUNG: 1a (both real lanes agree).

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s0 = mk("ab", "c")
    auto v = [c for c in s0 if c != mk("b", "")]
    print(v.len())
    print(v.get(0).unwrap())
